---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";

const title = "Pakistan Vehicle Token Tax Guide 2026: Punjab, Sindh & FBR Customs";
const description = "Guide to motor vehicle token tax in Pakistan across Punjab, Sindh, ICT, and KPK. View engine CC rates, applicable filer/non-filer information, and imported car customs duties.";
const image = "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1549399542-7e3f8b79c341?w=1200&q=80";
const canonical = "https://finsiva.com/blogs/pakistan-vehicle-tax-guide";
const author = "Sana Chaudhry";
const authorBio = "Automotive tax analyst specializing in provincial motor vehicle taxation, ePay online systems, and FBR custom duties.";
const lastUpdated = "August 2026";
const readTime = "15 min read";

const faqSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How is vehicle token tax calculated in Pakistan?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Vehicle token tax is calculated annually based on engine displacement capacity (CC), vehicle age, province of registration (Punjab, Sindh, ICT, KPK), and FBR Active Taxpayer (filer) status."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the custom duty on imported cars like Toyota Aqua, Honda Civic, and Vezel?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "Custom duty on imported vehicles is assessed under FBR customs valuation based on engine CC capacity (e.g., 1300cc, 1500cc, 1800cc), hybrid concessions, regulatory duty, and sales tax."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "How to pay motor vehicle token tax online in Sindh and Punjab?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "In Punjab, generate a PSID via ePay Punjab. In Sindh, generate a PSID on e-Payment GOS (excise.gos.pk) or MTMIS Sindh and pay via mobile banking apps."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is the advance withholding tax discount for active tax filers on vehicle purchases?",
      acceptedAnswer: {
        "@type": "Answer",
        text: "FBR active tax filers pay 50% or lower advance withholding tax on new motor vehicle registration and transfer compared to non-filers under Section 231B."
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<BlogLayout title={title} description={description} image={image} canonical={canonical} author={author} authorBio={authorBio} lastUpdated={lastUpdated} readTime={readTime}>
  <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">
            <p>
              Understanding <strong>pakistan vehicle tax</strong>, <strong>car tax rates karachi</strong>, <strong>sindh motor vehicle tax</strong>, and federal customs duties is essential for car buyers, vehicle owners, and commercial fleet operators.
            </p>
            <p>
              Vehicle taxation in Pakistan involves two distinct administrative levels: <strong>Provincial Excise & Taxation Departments</strong> (Punjab, Sindh, ICT, KPK, Balochistan) collecting annual token taxes and transfer fees, and <strong>Federal FBR</strong> collecting advance withholding taxes under Section 231B/234 and customs duties on vehicle imports.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">1. Provincial Excise Department Systems & Portals</h2>
            <p>
              Provincial excise departments collect annual token tax through integrated online portals:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Excise and Taxation Punjab (Lahore, Multan, Faisalabad, Rawalpindi)</strong>: Payments handled via <em>ePay Punjab</em> app generating 17-digit PSID numbers for online mobile banking.</li>
              <li><strong>Excise and Taxation Sindh (Karachi, Hyderabad)</strong>: Online verification via MTMIS Sindh and payment via e-Payment GOS (<code>excise.gos.pk</code>).</li>
              <li><strong>Excise and Taxation Islamabad (ICT)</strong>: Online token tax payments processed through the City Islamabad App.</li>
              <li><strong>Excise and Taxation KPK (Peshawar)</strong>: Online token tax verification via Zameen Dang / KP Excise portal.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">2. Annual Engine CC Token Tax Rates (2026)</h2>
            <p>
              Token tax schedules depend on engine displacement (CC):
            </p>

            <div class="my-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
              <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                <thead class="bg-canvas-soft border-b border-hairline dark:bg-surface/80 dark:border-overlay-lighter text-ink dark:text-on-primary font-bold">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="p-3">Engine Capacity (CC)</th>
                    <th class="p-3">Punjab / ICT Rate (Approx)</th>
                    <th class="p-3">Sindh Rate (Approx)</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline dark:divide-overlay-lighter">
                  <tr><td class="p-3 font-medium">Below 1000 CC (Alto, Cultus, WagonR)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-600">Lifetime Token Tax (PKR 10,000 - 15,000)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-emerald-600">Lifetime Token Tax</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3 font-medium">1001 CC to 1300 CC (Yaris, City)</td><td class="p-3">PKR 1,800 – 3,000 / year</td><td class="p-3">PKR 2,500 – 4,000 / year</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3 font-medium">1301 CC to 1500 CC (Civic, Elantra)</td><td class="p-3">PKR 3,500 – 6,000 / year</td><td class="p-3">PKR 4,500 – 7,500 / year</td></tr>
                  <tr><td class="p-3 font-medium">1501 CC to 2500 CC (Sportage, Tucson, Fortuner)</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">PKR 9,000 – 18,000 / year</td><td class="p-3 font-bold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">PKR 10,000 – 22,000 / year</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">How to Pay Vehicle Token Tax in Pakistan</h2>
            <p>
              Payment procedures for motor vehicle token tax vary by jurisdiction. Each province and federal territory operates its own Excise and Taxation portal or electronic payment system. Rates and payment procedures can change. Check the relevant provincial authority before making payment.
            </p>

            <div class="my-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">A. Punjab</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                  Administered through the <strong>Excise, Taxation & Narcotics Control Department Punjab</strong>. Vehicle owners can generate a 17-digit PSID and pay online via the official <a href="https://www.epay.punjab.gov.pk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">ePay Punjab Portal</a> or mobile app.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted dark:text-muted">
                  For official motor vehicle tax schedules and rules, visit the <a href="https://excise.punjab.gov.pk/motorvehicle_tax" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Punjab Excise Motor Vehicle Tax Portal</a>.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">B. Islamabad Capital Territory (ICT)</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                  Vehicle registration and token tax services for Islamabad are managed by <strong>Islamabad Excise & Taxation</strong>. Token tax payments can be initiated online via the City Islamabad mobile app or through official online payment channels.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted dark:text-muted">
                  Access official ICT vehicle services at the <a href="https://www.islamabadexcise.gov.pk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Islamabad Excise & Taxation Portal</a>.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">C. Sindh</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                  Administered by the <strong>Excise, Taxation & Narcotics Control Department Sindh</strong>. Owners in Karachi, Hyderabad, and other districts can verify vehicle records via MTMIS Sindh and generate PSID numbers for online payment via e-Payment GOS or participating banking apps.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted dark:text-muted">
                  Official services can be accessed at the <a href="https://excise.gos.pk/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Excise & Taxation Sindh Portal</a>.
                </p>
              </div>

              <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-5 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">D. Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP)</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
                  Administered through the provincial <strong>Excise, Taxation & Narcotics Control Department KP</strong>. Token tax verification and online payment options are available through official provincial e-services and mobile banking portals.
                </p>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-muted dark:text-muted">
                  Verify requirements with the KP Excise authority before making online payments.
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">What You Need Before Paying Token Tax</h2>
            <p>
              Before logging into your relevant provincial payment portal or banking app, gather the required vehicle details. Specific requirements vary by jurisdiction, but generally include:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">
              <li><strong>Vehicle Registration Number:</strong> Exact plate number and registration series.</li>
              <li><strong>Registration Jurisdiction:</strong> Province or territory where the vehicle is registered (e.g., Punjab, Sindh, ICT, KP).</li>
              <li><strong>Engine Capacity (CC):</strong> Engine displacement as listed on the registration smart card or book.</li>
              <li><strong>Applicable Tax Period:</strong> Current financial year for annual payment or lifetime verification details for under-1000cc vehicles.</li>
              <li><strong>Owner Identification:</strong> CNIC number of the registered owner or vehicle chassis number as required by the relevant portal.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Token Tax vs Other Vehicle Taxes & Fees</h2>
            <p>
              It is important to distinguish annual token tax from other charges associated with vehicle ownership and importation in Pakistan:
            </p>
            <div class="my-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
              <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
                <thead class="bg-canvas-soft border-b border-hairline dark:bg-surface/80 dark:border-overlay-lighter text-ink dark:text-on-primary font-bold">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="p-3">Tax / Fee Type</th>
                    <th class="p-3">Administering Body</th>
                    <th class="p-3">Purpose & Frequency</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="divide-y divide-hairline dark:divide-overlay-lighter">
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-medium">Motor Vehicle Token Tax</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Provincial Excise Dept</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Annual (or lifetime) tax for using public roads.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-medium">Initial Registration Fee</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Provincial Excise Dept</td>
                    <td class="p-3">One-time fee charged when issuing new plates and smart card.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-medium">Ownership Transfer Fee</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Provincial Excise Dept</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Fee charged when transferring vehicle title to a new owner.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-medium">FBR Advance Withholding Tax (Section 231B)</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Federal Board of Revenue (FBR)</td>
                    <td class="p-3">Advance income tax on new registration/transfer (50% discount for active filers).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td class="p-3 font-medium">Customs & Import Duty</td>
                    <td class="p-3">FBR Customs</td>
                    <td class="p-3">One-time import tax on C&F value for imported vehicles.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">3. Custom Duty on Imported Cars (Toyota Aqua, Civic, Vezel)</h2>
            <p>
              FBR levies heavy customs duties, regulatory duties, sales tax, and advance income tax on imported vehicles:
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li><strong>Custom Duty on Toyota Aqua (1500cc Hybrid)</strong>: Benefits from statutory hybrid concessions (50% concession for 1800cc hybrids under baggage/gift schemes), but total duty payable typically ranges between <strong>PKR 2.2M and PKR 3.0M</strong> depending on model year and grade.</li>
              <li><strong>Honda Vezel Custom Duty (1500cc Hybrid SUV)</strong>: Total import duty and taxes range between <strong>PKR 2.8M and PKR 3.6M</strong>.</li>
              <li><strong>Honda Civic Custom Duty (1500cc Turbo / 1800cc)</strong>: Commercial import duties exceed 100% of C&F value.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">4. FBR Advance Tax on New Car Registration (Section 231B)</h2>
            <p>
              When purchasing or registering a new motor vehicle, FBR collects advance withholding tax under Section 231B. Active tax filers enjoy a <strong>50% discount</strong> compared to non-filers.
            </p>
            <p>
              Calculate your vehicle token tax on our <a href="/countries/pakistan/vehicle-tax/vehicle-tax-calculator" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Vehicle Tax Calculator</a>, explore broader tax rules on the <a href="/countries/pakistan" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Tax Hub</a>, read our <a href="/blogs/pakistan-token-tax-guide" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Token Tax Guide</a> and <a href="/blogs/pakistan-sales-tax-guide" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Sales Tax Guide</a>, or visit the main <a href="/knowledge/pakistan-income-tax" class="text-link hover:underline dark:text-link">Pakistan Income Tax Overview</a>.
            </p>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
            {faqSchema.mainEntity.map(faq => (
              <div class="rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas p-6 dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">{faq.name}</h3>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted leading-relaxed">{faq.acceptedAnswer.text}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-canvas-soft border border-hairline dark:border-overlay-lighter dark:bg-surface">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-on-primary">About the Author</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm font-semibold text-primary dark:text-on-primary">{author}</p>
            <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-body dark:text-muted">{authorBio}</p>
  </div>
</BlogLayout>
